<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
        AUv2 .component entitlements
        ─────────────────────────────
        Classic AUv2 plug-ins are loaded in-process by the host application.
        They must NOT carry com.apple.security.app-sandbox: that flag causes the
        kernel to restrict the entire host process to the sandbox policy described
        here, which breaks non-sandboxed hosts (Logic Pro 10.7 and earlier, AULab,
        Reaper, etc.) and causes auval to fail with "sandbox deny file-read-data".

        For ad-hoc (-) signing no entitlements file is needed at all; this file
        exists so that codesign can be invoked consistently regardless of identity.
        If you sign with a Developer ID Application identity add only the minimum
        required entitlements here (e.g. com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory
        if your DSP kernel requires it for JIT/SIMD, but ArpSID does not).
    -->
</dict>
</plist>
